flowchart LR
    Inner["inner Ethernet frame<br/><b>does:</b> carries tenant src/dst MAC/IP<br/><b>why next:</b> VXLAN device must map overlay destination<br/><b>state:</b> skb belongs to overlay netdev"]
    FDB["VXLAN FDB / VNI lookup<br/><b>does:</b> maps inner dst MAC + VNI to remote VTEP<br/><b>why next:</b> underlay needs an outer IP destination<br/><b>state:</b> selected VNI and VTEP IP"]
    Encap["encapsulation<br/><b>does:</b> prepends outer Ethernet/IP/UDP + VXLAN header<br/><b>why next:</b> underlay routers only understand outer packet<br/><b>state:</b> skb now contains tunnel metadata and outer headers"]
    Underlay["underlay route output<br/><b>does:</b> routes outer IP packet to remote VTEP<br/><b>why next:</b> NIC transmits ordinary UDP/IP frame<br/><b>state:</b> outer nexthop/dev selected"]
    Wire["wire<br/><b>state:</b> UDP dst port 4789, VNI identifies tenant segment"]
    UDP["remote UDP tunnel socket<br/><b>does:</b> receives port 4789 and dispatches to VXLAN handler<br/><b>why next:</b> VXLAN code validates header/VNI<br/><b>state:</b> encapsulated skb accepted by tunnel endpoint"]
    Decap["decapsulation<br/><b>does:</b> removes outer headers and restores inner frame context<br/><b>why next:</b> bridge/IP stack should see original tenant frame<br/><b>state:</b> skb attached to VXLAN netdev RX path"]
    Stack["normal RX path<br/><b>does:</b> bridge, IP, netfilter, or socket delivery handles inner frame<br/><b>state:</b> tenant packet behaves as local L2 traffic"]

    Inner --> FDB --> Encap --> Underlay --> Wire --> UDP --> Decap --> Stack

    classDef overlay fill:#dbeafe,stroke:#2563eb
    classDef tunnel fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#d97706
    classDef underlay fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#16a34a
    class Inner,FDB,Stack overlay
    class Encap,UDP,Decap tunnel
    class Underlay,Wire underlay
